ll did he know how to take a correct  angle  he get behind a ball could he pivot his  hips could he play through a ball and  make a strong throw and the answer to  that was no the froze were on a 20 to 80  scale of my opinion the arm strength out  of 40 just below average we factor in  the ability to get to a bag accurately  that was a struggle for him at one point  in time he fell in the outfield on the  warning track and I was taken aback by  that when you consider the footwork  required to play the position of  quarterback whether it be at the  collegiate level or the NFL but then you  have to remind yourself that Tim Tebow  was not the prototypical quarterback at  the collegiate level or the NFL level  this is a man who for lack of a better  term outmuscled the game for the most  part of his career think about baseball  Dan you can outmuscle this game it  doesn't care how big you are how strong  you are how tall you are how fast you  are if you can't apply any of those  skills to the skill set required to  achieve success in the game of baseball  you're done you don't even get to start  what kind of pitches would you throw him  well it all depends on what side of the  tebow camp I was on if I was receding  you're facing him you're you're actually  facing after you know he hit fast balls  but if you were actually facing him what  would download right make him if I face  Tim Tebow he's going to get my 85 287 a  two-seamer running in on the hands  probably somewhere in the upper echelon  of the strike zone and then he's going  to get the sliders down in a way because  he hasn't seen one since he's 16 and  he's not going to have a chance to get  to it that's just going to be that's  just the truth that's that's the nuts  and bolts of the situation you run him  in but you put him in that proverbial  rocking chair hard in soft away his role  a wrinkle on them thanks for coming out  I feel like a team would want to be if  I'm a team then let's say you're the  Padres or